{
  "rationale": "The plant models robot perception and motion capabilities, separating sensor outcomes and motion commands. The specification automata enforce safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are chosen conservatively after obstacle events. Full_rotate is only used as a last-resort in deadlock recovery. All obstacle events force a turn before returning to exploration. The design avoids oscillations and infinite loops, and ensures steady progress with reliable collision avoidance.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion, with all events explicit and deterministic.",
    "Specification automata bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration."
  ],
